<h2 class="g-h2" id="in-the-app">Inside the app</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p><strong>Copy page</strong> exports a complete Eleventy page. Save it as <code>src/examples/&lt;name&gt;.njk</code> in the app, then build. The payload includes the base layout, page scripts, macro imports and data setup. Keep those parts when adapting its body into an existing template; do not paste its front matter into an include.</p>
  <p>Record-backed pages select an explicit preview id from <code>allOpinions</code> with a portable Nunjucks loop. Set <code>exampleOpinionId</code> to your own available record. Missing records or evidence render a setup message. Chart fixtures are labelled illustrative and copied as literal rows, with the app's <code>chartBreakdown</code> filter; neither <code>opinionById</code> nor guide-only data is needed.</p>
  <p>Some fragments depend on the full reader's tabs, panel and callbacks. Those exports are labelled <em>Reader composition</em> and include the real <code>partials/opinion-page.njk</code> host with its scripts. The isolated fragment's source path remains above the code. Visual-state exports are labelled separately and do not promise application actions.</p>
</div>
